    name: 'Premium Home Service Fake Local Business Directory Scheme',
    slug: 'illinois-premium-home-service-fake-business-directory-scheme',
    description: `B.E.S.T. GDR LLC, doing business as Premium Home Service and run by CEO Yosef Bernath out of Westchester, Illinois, built thousands of fake online business profiles for home-repair companies that did not actually exist, maintaining more than 7,600 phone numbers across over 250 area codes and using search engine optimization to make the fake listings rank as though they were real local businesses. Consumers searching for a nearby plumber, HVAC technician, or appliance repair company would call what looked like a local number, only to be routed to overseas call-center representatives who sold a paid "membership" or service-call fee and then outsourced the actual job to unqualified third-party providers with no connection to the business the consumer thought they were hiring. Illinois Attorney General Kwame Raoul, joined by the U.S. Department of Justice, sued Premium Home Service and Bernath on May 11, 2026, alleging the scheme had defrauded more than 100,000 consumers nationwide since at least 2018. "Premium Home Service spent years establishing fake businesses with fake reviews to lure in customers who were in need of home repairs," Raoul said. The lawsuit seeks a permanent injunction, civil penalties, and monetary compensation for affected consumers. Anyone searching online for a local repair service is advised to check whether the business has a verifiable physical address and a consistent name across the phone listing, the website, and any invoice, to be wary of a company that asks for a membership fee before diagnosing the problem, and to search the business name alongside the word "complaints" or check it on the Better Business Bureau's site before paying anything.`,
